==== VLAN Tagging for WAN ====
Note that the WAN port is connected to eth1 and not eth0, and that the LUCI web interface does not list eth1 for VLANs.\\
To tag the WAN port create the VLAN ID under "Network => Switch" and assign it to "CPU".
Under "Network => Interface" edit the "WAN" interface and use for its "Physical Settings" the "Custom Interface": eth1.<VLAN ID>\\
Example: VLAN ID 7 for German Telekom VDSL would be eth1.7

==== Sample Single DMZ Port Configuration ====

This configuration demonstrates configuring a single port ([[#network_port_assignments|LAN 1 / Port 3]])
on the WZR-HP-G300NH as a DMZ using the rtl8366s switch.

:!: **Do not forget** to follow the [[docs:guide-user:firewall:dmz#setting_up_the_firewall|Firewall DMZ setup guide]] if you want your DMZ to be of any use.

<code>config 'interface' 'loopback'
	option 'ifname' 'lo'
	option 'proto' 'static'
	option 'ipaddr' '127.0.0.1'
	option 'netmask' '255.0.0.0'

config 'interface' 'lan'
	option 'ifname' 'eth0.1'
	option 'type' 'bridge'
	option 'proto' 'static'
	option 'ipaddr' '192.168.1.1'
	option 'netmask' '255.255.255.0'

config 'interface' 'wan'
	option 'ifname' 'eth1'
	option 'proto' 'pppoe'
	option 'username' '-------'
	option 'password' '-------'

config 'switch'
	option 'name' 'rtl8366s'
        option 'enable' '1'
        option 'enable_vlan' '1'
        option 'reset' '1'

config 'switch_vlan' 'eth0_1'
	option 'device' 'rtl8366s'
	option 'vlan' '1'
	option 'ports' '0 1 2 5t'

config 'switch_vlan' 'eth0_2'
	option 'device' 'rtl8366s'
	option 'vlan' '2'
	option 'ports' '3 5t'

config 'interface' 'dmz'
       option 'ifname' 'eth0.2'
       option 'proto' 'static'
       option 'ipaddr' 192.168.2.1
       option 'netmask' 255.255.255.0</code>



